## Class Reflection

## Progress Made in This Session

The emphasis for today's session was getting the application up and running from the rudimentary project configuration to its implementation. We designed splash screen and main notes screen and began linking to the various sections of the program.

More functionality was added to the splash screen. To give the user an idea of what the application was doing as it launched, we created a progress bar as well as added some loading messages, such as the “Loading saved notes...” message. We also implemented the last-opened-time feature and added a close button that could be used while the application was loading.

## Main Application Development

After completing the splash screen, we started creating the main application screen using FXML. A text box was included to enable users to enter their notes.

The main functionality of saving notes was then implemented. We also worked on loading the previously saved notes when the application was opened again. That was very helpful as the user would not lose his/her previous work after closing the application.

## Handling Unsaved Changes

One of the other key features we were tackling was unsaved changes detection. The application could detect if the user had made changes to a note that they had not saved. A warning could then be displayed before the application is closed in order to avoid the loss of the user's work.

This gave me the idea that an application should not only cater for the normal usage flow but also if an unanticipated event like closing by accident occurred.

