In this session, we linked the splash screen to the main application screen in such a way that the application would be loaded to the actual notes screen.

We were also able to link the FXML components to the Java controller and application logic. This helped me to appreciate how the interface which I had created in FXML was related to the java code which makes the interface functional.

## Testing and Improvements

We have tested the app numerous times, from the splash screen to the main notes screen. While testing, we noticed areas that needed corrections and made adjustments to improve the overall layout and appearance.

This was helpful as some features were tested singly and had to be retested when they were integrated into the full application.

## What I Learned

In this session, I learned about the different features that can be integrated to make a working application. I came to understand that there are lots of little components that must be linked to the Java code behind the program, such as the interface, buttons, text area, saving system, loading system and warnings.

I also learned to understand the importance of testing after implementing multiple features as there are small issues that might become apparent when different components of the application interact with each other.

## Challenges During Development

The biggest problem was ensuring that all the features performed in a harmonious manner. The implementation of the splash screen and the main screen, and the binding of the FXML components to the controller was a careful task.

Rather than that, thinking about different scenarios where users might interact with the application was required when handling saved notes and detecting unsaved changes.

## Reflection

This session was more of a “real” development session, rather than just preparing the structure as in the previous session. Now, we could begin to see the app working as a fully fledged notes app.

The repeated testing did reveal to me another aspect of development that is not a one-time only. Once we had implemented a feature, we had to run it and identify any problems to make corrections, and then test again. In general, this session made me understand the relationship among the various JavaFX concepts, which then makes a functional application.

## Key Takeaways

1. A splash screen can have graphics as well as useful loading functionality.
2. Correct linking between FXML components, controllers and Java code.
3. The ability to save and load data lets users work with notes they create in the past.
4. Unsaved-change warning: Reduces accidental loss of user work. 
5. Testing the complete application flow is important after combining multiple features.
